#### Rating comparisons

> ℹ️ `self_rating_avg`, `manager_rating_avg`, `practice_manager_rating_avg`, and `rating_self_mgr_gap` are pre-computed employee-level averages stored in the index (average across all objectives). A positive `rating_self_mgr_gap` means the employee rated themselves higher than the manager. For 2026, `manager_rating_avg` and `rating_self_mgr_gap` will be `\N` if the manager has not yet finalized ratings.

| Question pattern | `fields` to use |
|---|---|
| "self-rating vs manager rating" / "comparison of ratings" / "self vs mgr" / "highlight self-assessment outliers" | `emp_name,self_rating_avg,manager_rating_avg,rating_self_mgr_gap,category_band,manager_validated_final_kra_score` |
| "practice manager rating comparison" | `emp_name,self_rating_avg,manager_rating_avg,practice_manager_rating_avg,rating_self_mgr_gap,category_band,manager_validated_final_kra_score` |
| "performance summary of all reportees" / "overall ratings for team" | `emp_name,category_band,manager_validated_final_kra_score,self_rating_avg,manager_rating_avg,rating_self_mgr_gap,separation_status` |

