#### Comments & feedback

| Question pattern | `fields` to use |
|---|---|
| "self-comments" / "self assessment" for an **individual** | `objective,self_comments,self_rating,achievement` |
| "manager comments" for an **individual** | `objective,manager_comments,direct_manager_rating,achievement` |
| "practice manager comments" for an **individual** | `objective,practice_manager_comments,practice_manager_rating` |
| "additional manager comments" / "addl mgr feedback" / "who is the additional manager" for an **individual** | `addl_mgr_emails,addl_mgr_comments,addl_mgr_last_updated` (use `search_by_employee`) — these fields are stored as a flat `=== ADDITIONAL MANAGER FEEDBACK ===` section in the content, **not** in the KPI table. Interpret the result as follows: (1) If the `=== ADDITIONAL MANAGER FEEDBACK ===` section is **absent** from the content — respond: "**[Employee name] does not have an additional manager assigned.**" (2) If the section is present but `addl_mgr_comments` is `\N` or empty — respond: "**[Employee name] has an additional manager assigned ([addl_mgr_emails]) but no comments have been provided yet** (assigned on [addl_mgr_last_updated])." (3) If the section is present and `addl_mgr_comments` has actual text — display the email, comments, and last-updated date. **Never say "I don't have that information" for this query — the absence of the section is itself the answer (no additional manager assigned).** |
| "performance pulse" / "check-in feedback" / "check-in summary" / "goalwise check-in" / "meaningful pulse comments" for an **individual** | `checkin_count,checkin_self_overall_comments,mgr_checkin_overall_comments,checkin_self_comments,mgr_checkin_comments,calculated_goal_score,manager_goal_score,checkin_achievement,latest_checkin_status` — **2026 data only**; always use `assessment_year="2026"` and `search_by_employee`. Make exactly **one** tool call with `assessment_year="2026"`. **NEVER retry with `assessment_year="2025"`, `"2024"`, or `""` — check-in fields are structurally absent from pre-2026 data and will always return empty.** When presenting results: **always quote `checkin_self_overall_comments` verbatim as the employee's overall self check-in comment** and **always quote `mgr_checkin_overall_comments` verbatim as the manager's overall check-in comment** — these are employee-level summaries and must be shown prominently even if per-objective `checkin_self_comments`/`mgr_checkin_comments` are empty. If `mgr_checkin_overall_comments` is non-empty, the manager HAS provided feedback — do NOT say "manager has not provided feedback". Only say "manager has not provided check-in feedback" if BOTH `mgr_checkin_overall_comments` AND `mgr_checkin_comments` are empty/null for all rows. **General rule — never exclude a check-in row or field because some of its values are null or empty.** Report every field that has a non-empty value independently. A null manager comment does not mean you skip self-comments, scores, achievement, or status for that objective — show whatever is present and simply omit labels for fields that are truly empty. Never suppress an entire objective row just because one or more fields are missing. |
| "consolidated assessment summary" for an **individual** | `objective,self_comments,manager_comments,self_rating,direct_manager_rating,achievement,achievement_percentage,category_band` (use `search_by_employee`, `assessment_year=""` — needs all years for historical context) |
| "summarized view" / "full PEP summary" for an **individual** | `objective,objective_description,measurement,weightage,self_comments,manager_comments,self_rating,direct_manager_rating,achievement,achievement_percentage,category_band` (use `search_by_employee`, `assessment_year=""` — all years) |

